cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VectorSmuggle in your work, please cite the companion preprint and the software framework."
type: software
title: "VectorSmuggle: A research framework for vector-based data exfiltration"
authors:
  - family-names: Wanger
    given-names: Jascha
    affiliation: "Tarnover, LLC"
abstract: >-
  VectorSmuggle is the research framework that accompanies the preprint
  "VectorSmuggle: Steganographic Exfiltration in Embedding Stores and a
  Cryptographic Provenance Defense." It implements six steganographic
  techniques against vector embedding stores, the empirical evaluation
  pipeline (rotation sweep, paraphrased-query retrieval, cross-backend
  round-trip, adaptive-attacker detector studies), and the defensive
  baselines used in the paper.
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jaschadub/VectorSmuggle"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "VectorSmuggle: Steganographic Exfiltration in Embedding Stores and a Cryptographic Provenance Defense"
  authors:
    - family-names: Wanger
      given-names: Jascha
      affiliation: "ThirdKey / Tarnover, LLC"
  year: 2026
  doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20058256"
  url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20058256"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "VectorPin: Verifiable integrity for AI embedding stores"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wanger
        given-names: Jascha
    license: Apache-2.0
    url: "https://github.com/ThirdKeyAI/VectorPin"
    notes: "Defensive cryptographic-provenance protocol motivated by the empirical findings in this repo."
